WEBVTT

00:00:01.880 --> 00:00:05.710
Ms. Iris's father and Ms. Kate's mother...?!

00:00:08.250 --> 00:00:11.040
This is my first time seeing someone
from a different race...

00:00:11.750 --> 00:00:16.040
So this is where you were
after all, Iris and Kate.

00:00:16.500 --> 00:00:18.830
What are you two doing here, Father?

00:00:19.580 --> 00:00:21.830
Well, you see...

00:00:22.710 --> 00:00:26.170
Um, if you don't mind,
please come on inside.

00:00:26.170 --> 00:00:27.500
You don't mind?

00:00:27.500 --> 00:00:30.420
There's no need to just stand
around here while talking, right?

00:00:32.210 --> 00:00:33.420
You have my gratitude.

00:00:33.420 --> 00:00:34.880
Pardon us.

00:00:35.170 --> 00:00:36.420
Please, come this way!

00:00:36.420 --> 00:00:37.420
Right...

00:00:45.670 --> 00:00:49.830
Kyou kara mieru yo chiisai hoshi

00:00:49.830 --> 00:00:53.250
Terashitete ne mune no naka o

00:00:53.250 --> 00:00:56.540
Naite waratte kagaiyaite

00:00:56.540 --> 00:00:58.750
Udemakutte arukidasou

00:00:58.750 --> 00:01:01.960
(Kitto alright nayamu wa go sign)

00:01:01.960 --> 00:01:04.250
(Kichin to yarimashou)

00:01:05.710 --> 00:01:11.630
Jiyuu sugiru tte nante fujiyuu nan deshou

00:01:11.630 --> 00:01:14.960
Datte tokenai no yo

00:01:14.960 --> 00:01:18.380
Rironchi jikkenchi spiral

00:01:18.830 --> 00:01:20.460
Maido utedo katte mo

00:01:20.460 --> 00:01:22.040
(Nani o tameshite mite mo)

00:01:22.040 --> 00:01:23.710
Nengan kanatte shikuhakku

00:01:23.710 --> 00:01:25.540
(Cheat ja nai yo life hack)

00:01:25.540 --> 00:01:29.000
Harete ippo fumidaseru license

00:01:29.000 --> 00:01:31.250
Kore kara ga hajimari

00:01:31.420 --> 00:01:35.500
Kyou kara mieru yo chiisai hoshi

00:01:35.500 --> 00:01:38.880
Terashitete ne mune no naka o

00:01:38.880 --> 00:01:42.250
Naite waratte kagaiyaite

00:01:42.250 --> 00:01:44.880
Shigoto no mae wa shinkokyuu

00:01:44.880 --> 00:01:49.040
Hibike te o nobashita shintenchi

00:01:49.040 --> 00:01:52.380
Yume wa kitto te no naka

00:01:52.380 --> 00:01:55.790
Kitto dekiru original

00:01:55.790 --> 00:01:58.500
Door o akete welcome de ikou

00:01:58.500 --> 00:02:01.000
(Sore ja koko ga start)

00:02:01.000 --> 00:02:04.500
(Kitto alright nayamu wa go sign)

00:02:04.500 --> 00:02:06.920
(Kichin to yarimashou)

00:02:10.040 --> 00:02:13.000
My deepest apologies
for intruding so suddenly.

00:02:13.500 --> 00:02:17.330
I am Adelbert Lotze, Iris's father.

00:02:17.960 --> 00:02:23.500
And I'm Caterina Starven, Kate's mom,
and I serve the house of Lotze.

00:02:24.040 --> 00:02:27.420
I'm Sarasa Feed, this shop's owner.

00:02:27.830 --> 00:02:31.830
I have heard tell of how you helped
our daughters, Lady Sarasa.

00:02:31.830 --> 00:02:32.960
You have my gratitude.

00:02:32.960 --> 00:02:34.250
Thank you.

00:02:34.250 --> 00:02:36.380
I-it's nothing...

00:02:36.580 --> 00:02:39.000
So you were a noble, Ms. Iris...?

00:02:39.000 --> 00:02:40.790
It isn't as if I was hiding it!

00:02:40.790 --> 00:02:43.290
I didn't want everyone to act
on guard around me!

00:02:43.290 --> 00:02:47.670
And even if we are nobles, it's just a
knighthood with two villages of territory,

00:02:47.670 --> 00:02:49.290
hardly nobles at all!

00:02:49.290 --> 00:02:52.250
Iris, you could stand to choose
your words a bit more carefully...

00:02:53.290 --> 00:02:55.290
A-ah, my apologies...

00:02:55.880 --> 00:02:59.330
So, what brings you here, Sir Adelbert...?

00:02:59.330 --> 00:03:00.380
Well...

00:03:02.130 --> 00:03:05.080
Iris, we've come to get you.

00:03:05.380 --> 00:03:06.670
To get me?!

00:03:11.290 --> 00:03:14.330
Um, should I excuse myself...?

00:03:14.330 --> 00:03:16.670
No, please stay, Ms. Owner.

00:03:17.080 --> 00:03:19.540
I would rather you know everything,

00:03:19.540 --> 00:03:22.130
than burden you with
some vague concerns.

00:03:22.130 --> 00:03:24.250
Well then, I'll go handle the shop.

00:03:24.250 --> 00:03:25.540
Right, please do.

00:03:25.540 --> 00:03:27.040
My apologies, Lorea...

00:03:27.040 --> 00:03:29.040
It's fine. Excuse me.

00:03:31.630 --> 00:03:34.960
Well then, could I ask you
to explain, Ms. Iris?

00:03:35.630 --> 00:03:38.130
I would need to begin by
telling you of the circumstances

00:03:38.130 --> 00:03:41.170
that led to us becoming
gatherers in the first place.

00:03:42.380 --> 00:03:46.210
Though the house of Lotze are nobles,
it isn't as if we were ever well off.

00:03:46.210 --> 00:03:50.500
But father was adored by his people,
and our territory was a peaceful place.

00:03:51.250 --> 00:03:54.420
One year, though, the territory
suffered terrible crop failure.

00:03:54.880 --> 00:03:58.920
And so, Father reduced all taxes
for the sake of his suffering people.

00:03:58.920 --> 00:04:00.960
On top of that,
he used his personal finances

00:04:00.960 --> 00:04:04.000
to purchase up food for them
in order to provide assistance.

00:04:04.500 --> 00:04:07.040
However, his fortune soon bottomed out,

00:04:07.040 --> 00:04:10.540
and our house ended up burdened with
a terribly great deal of debt.

00:04:11.250 --> 00:04:13.830
So even as the lord of the land,
you took on the debt personally?

00:04:13.830 --> 00:04:15.960
And you're saying it was
no trivial amount...?

00:04:17.880 --> 00:04:21.880
The one in charge of that debt
was Baronet Yokuo Kirk,

00:04:21.880 --> 00:04:25.880
who rules South Straug and Yok Village.

00:04:26.420 --> 00:04:29.960
Eventually we overcame
that predicament, however...

00:04:30.250 --> 00:04:34.000
It took some time for the lives of
the residents to stabilize.

00:04:34.000 --> 00:04:38.830
And in the meantime, it was all we could
manage to pay off the interest.

00:04:39.540 --> 00:04:44.330
So to help out at least a little with all that,
Iris became a gatherer.

00:04:44.790 --> 00:04:48.380
She didn't concern herself with the danger,
even as a noble's daughter.

00:04:48.380 --> 00:04:49.880
I just...

00:04:50.170 --> 00:04:54.460
I wanted to teach a lesson
to that Baronet Kirk,

00:04:54.460 --> 00:04:58.580
who took advantage of our situation
to force unreasonable interest rates!

00:05:02.920 --> 00:05:06.330
And Kate went and came along with me...

00:05:06.580 --> 00:05:08.460
But Sir Adelbert,

00:05:08.460 --> 00:05:13.750
weren't the residents helping out
so that you could pay it off bit by bit?

00:05:13.750 --> 00:05:14.830
That's true!

00:05:14.830 --> 00:05:17.130
So why are you coming for me now?

00:05:17.460 --> 00:05:19.460
The circumstances have changed...

00:05:20.080 --> 00:05:23.000
They're demanding a full repayment
of the debt all at once.

00:05:23.000 --> 00:05:24.750
A full repayment?

00:05:25.330 --> 00:05:28.210
They were already forcing
a high interest rate,

00:05:28.210 --> 00:05:30.670
and now this...?!

00:05:30.960 --> 00:05:34.420
We long since passed the usual
time limit for repayment,

00:05:34.420 --> 00:05:36.040
so we cannot complain.

00:05:36.420 --> 00:05:40.290
I've tried every means possible
in order to gather the money.

00:05:40.290 --> 00:05:45.420
But it isn't so easy to get
ahold of so great a sum.

00:05:45.920 --> 00:05:47.040
However...

00:05:47.580 --> 00:05:51.210
A single person willing to loan us
the money came forward.

00:05:52.830 --> 00:05:54.130
And yet...

00:05:54.130 --> 00:05:56.380
It came with conditions, right?

00:05:57.960 --> 00:06:00.250
I see... So that's it.

00:06:00.250 --> 00:06:04.750
I had intended to be prepared for
this day to come at any time, but...

00:06:04.960 --> 00:06:07.630
Huh? What are you talking about?

00:06:08.170 --> 00:06:11.380
The one who I consulted with
was a certain company

00:06:11.380 --> 00:06:13.880
that has been expanding
their business extensively.

00:06:14.040 --> 00:06:16.830
Due to a recent sudden death
the owner has changed,

00:06:16.830 --> 00:06:19.830
with a young successor
now taking charge.

00:06:20.250 --> 00:06:24.750
The man in question wishes to marry
into the house of Lotze.

00:06:25.000 --> 00:06:26.540
Marry?!

00:06:26.540 --> 00:06:31.580
In other words, the condition for
the loan is a marriage with me...

00:06:33.630 --> 00:06:36.880
As I am a noble's daughter,
there's no helping that.

00:06:36.880 --> 00:06:39.540
Are you really alright with that, Iris?!

00:06:39.540 --> 00:06:41.460
Control yourself, Kate.

00:06:41.460 --> 00:06:42.330
But...!

00:06:42.670 --> 00:06:45.670
And Sir Adelbert,
can you truly accept this?

00:06:45.670 --> 00:06:47.540
Even if it is for your residents,

00:06:47.540 --> 00:06:51.710
accepting the marriage means allowing
a merchant to steal away your estate...

00:06:51.710 --> 00:06:52.710
Kate!

00:06:55.460 --> 00:06:59.500
Naturally, I am not thrilled with
the matter myself.

00:06:59.830 --> 00:07:03.420
But he cannot be so bad of a person

00:07:03.420 --> 00:07:07.960
if he is willing to shoulder the debt
of such a minor noble house.

00:07:08.710 --> 00:07:09.630
Right...

00:07:09.920 --> 00:07:13.210
And if he has money, there may not
be any need to go into debt

00:07:13.210 --> 00:07:16.330
even if another crop shortage
arises in the future.

00:07:16.330 --> 00:07:17.580
Iris...

00:07:17.880 --> 00:07:21.210
So, what sort of man is he?

00:07:21.460 --> 00:07:23.250
Well, I have only met him the once,

00:07:23.250 --> 00:07:25.420
but he seemed a rather
agreeable young man.

00:07:25.420 --> 00:07:27.130
His name is Shay Dilly.

00:07:27.330 --> 00:07:28.540
Dilly...?

00:07:29.210 --> 00:07:33.290
So the company offering to lend you
money is the Dilly Company?

00:07:34.500 --> 00:07:39.210
That's the one we just quarreled with
over the frostfang bat fangs...

00:07:39.210 --> 00:07:41.000
That's Gree Dilly's company!

00:07:41.420 --> 00:07:42.830
You know of them?

00:07:42.830 --> 00:07:46.880
A lot happened between us and
the Dilly Company not that long ago.

00:07:46.880 --> 00:07:50.290
So let me just say, something seems
a bit out of sorts about all of this.

00:07:50.290 --> 00:07:54.920
To be blunt, I can't imagine that
they have the capital needed

00:07:54.920 --> 00:07:58.290
to lend out a large sum
of money right now.

00:07:58.500 --> 00:07:59.630
That's right!

00:07:59.630 --> 00:08:01.630
They're definitely up to something!

00:08:03.080 --> 00:08:06.920
But the current head of the Dilly house
seemed a fine young man...

00:08:07.210 --> 00:08:10.790
They say that no swindler ever allows
themself to appear all that bad.

00:08:10.790 --> 00:08:14.580
Yet we are nothing but an
insignificant minor noble house.

00:08:14.580 --> 00:08:16.290
Why approach us?

00:08:17.210 --> 00:08:20.080
Even a knighthood counts
as proper nobility.

00:08:20.080 --> 00:08:22.750
There's plenty of value there
for a merchant.

00:08:22.750 --> 00:08:28.040
And though I can't say for certain,
Baronet Kirk may be involved too...

00:08:28.250 --> 00:08:29.330
Unbelievable...!

00:08:29.500 --> 00:08:32.710
Ah, but that's ultimately just
speculation on my part.

00:08:32.710 --> 00:08:36.460
I'll have an acquaintance in South Straug
look into the matter later.

00:08:37.290 --> 00:08:38.710
Sir Adelbert...

00:08:40.210 --> 00:08:42.170
Just as you say, Lady Sarasa,

00:08:42.170 --> 00:08:44.790
it seems we need to
investigate this matter further.

00:08:45.330 --> 00:08:47.960
But even if they truly can
prepare the money,

00:08:47.960 --> 00:08:49.920
I have no intention of allowing
someone so suspicious

00:08:49.920 --> 00:08:52.040
enter into our house of Lotze!

00:08:52.250 --> 00:08:53.750
Sir Adelbert!

00:08:54.250 --> 00:08:57.130
But what about the debt, Father...?

00:08:57.130 --> 00:08:58.710
Ah, yes...

00:08:58.960 --> 00:09:01.790
Our circumstances haven't
changed in the least.

00:09:01.790 --> 00:09:02.920
No...

00:09:03.460 --> 00:09:09.380
Learning of these suspicions regarding
Baronet Kirk and the Dilly Company is huge.

00:09:09.380 --> 00:09:10.290
Indeed.

00:09:10.290 --> 00:09:12.290
We shall steadily work to raise money

00:09:12.290 --> 00:09:14.580
rather than leaping at an opportunity
that seemed too good to believe...

00:09:14.580 --> 00:09:16.580
This may well be a divine revolution.

00:09:16.880 --> 00:09:19.000
We'll work the problem over again
from the start!

00:09:19.000 --> 00:09:21.130
We're heading back to our land!

00:09:21.130 --> 00:09:22.130
Right!

00:09:22.420 --> 00:09:23.420
Father!

00:09:23.880 --> 00:09:26.330
So I needn't return home?

00:09:26.330 --> 00:09:30.670
Yes, we shall still be counting on
what you can send for the time being.

00:09:30.670 --> 00:09:34.080
But you needn't worry any further.

00:09:35.210 --> 00:09:37.170
My apologies for being such a
good-for-nothing father.

00:09:37.170 --> 00:09:38.290
Ah, no!

00:09:38.290 --> 00:09:42.170
No matter how far apart we may be,

00:09:42.170 --> 00:09:44.290
I'll always be proud to be your daughter.

00:09:44.290 --> 00:09:48.580
Mama, I'll be working way harder
as a gatherer too!

00:09:48.580 --> 00:09:50.580
Thanks, Kate.

00:09:51.420 --> 00:09:55.080
But make sure that you take care of yourself.

00:09:55.080 --> 00:09:56.080
Yeah...

00:09:56.460 --> 00:09:58.790
You too, Mama.

00:10:02.040 --> 00:10:07.580
Lady Sarasa, my deepest apologies for
troubling you so over our family matters.

00:10:08.080 --> 00:10:11.040
Please continue to
look after Iris and Kate.

00:10:11.040 --> 00:10:12.790
Yes, of course.

00:10:12.790 --> 00:10:15.000
And I look forward to
seeing you again as well!

00:10:15.460 --> 00:10:16.750
Well then, farewell.

00:10:17.330 --> 00:10:19.960
This has truly turned out to be
a worthwhile trip!

00:10:34.630 --> 00:10:38.170
Still, is everything
really going to be alright...?

00:10:39.960 --> 00:10:42.420
Right... Sir Adelbert must have been

00:10:42.420 --> 00:10:46.500
seriously conflicted about
bringing this matter to us.

00:10:46.500 --> 00:10:49.630
So for him to still feel
the need to come in the end...

00:10:49.880 --> 00:10:53.630
Yes, he must be very much
at his wits' end.

00:10:53.630 --> 00:10:54.630
Yeah...

00:10:55.880 --> 00:10:56.960
Ms. Owner!

00:10:57.540 --> 00:10:58.710
My apologies!

00:10:58.710 --> 00:11:00.130
Huh? What for?

00:11:00.130 --> 00:11:04.460
For being unable to bring up
my debt to you at that time.

00:11:04.460 --> 00:11:08.920
I of course had no intention of running out
on my bill and returning home...

00:11:08.920 --> 00:11:14.000
To be honest, we actually haven't let them
know the amount that we owe.

00:11:14.000 --> 00:11:18.460
Telling them that would mean
informing them of how I almost died.

00:11:18.750 --> 00:11:22.290
And we didn't want to add on
further worries for our parents.

00:11:22.500 --> 00:11:23.790
I truly am sorry.

00:11:24.000 --> 00:11:25.960
Oh no, please don't worry about it.

00:11:26.380 --> 00:11:29.540
But more importantly, it sounds like
your family's had it really rough.

00:11:29.540 --> 00:11:32.250
Please don't worry about
paying me back for now,

00:11:32.250 --> 00:11:34.880
and just send them
whatever you can instead.

00:11:35.000 --> 00:11:38.210
If it comes down to it,
I can always ask my master...

00:11:38.210 --> 00:11:39.790
No, you mustn't!

00:11:39.790 --> 00:11:42.210
You should keep her separate from this!

00:11:42.210 --> 00:11:43.210
But...

00:11:43.210 --> 00:11:44.210
I...

00:11:44.790 --> 00:11:48.000
I want to do something to help out too.

00:11:48.000 --> 00:11:49.080
Lorea...

00:11:49.580 --> 00:11:54.540
But all I can do is help out
my own family and Ms. Sarasa,

00:11:54.540 --> 00:11:58.330
and just try my hardest.

00:11:58.830 --> 00:12:00.250
Lorea...!

00:12:00.250 --> 00:12:01.670
Thank you!

00:12:02.080 --> 00:12:07.040
I shall also try my hardest,
in order to repay that sentiment!

00:12:07.040 --> 00:12:09.540
Trying your hardest...

00:12:10.000 --> 00:12:11.290
That's it!

00:12:12.460 --> 00:12:15.630
Right, I'm an alchemist
and a shop owner!

00:12:15.630 --> 00:12:17.830
And you two are gatherers!

00:12:17.830 --> 00:12:20.830
So we've just got to do
everything that we can!

00:12:20.830 --> 00:12:22.420
What we can...?

00:12:22.580 --> 00:12:24.330
I mean gathering ingredients!

00:12:24.330 --> 00:12:26.580
Ones that can sell for as much as possible!

00:12:26.750 --> 00:12:29.960
I won't say it's a shortcut to amassing
a great fortune or anything,

00:12:29.960 --> 00:12:34.170
but it's the best method available to us!

00:12:34.170 --> 00:12:37.630
Yes, you're right!
It's just as you say, Ms. Owner!

00:12:37.630 --> 00:12:39.920
Yeah! Let's give it all we've got, Iris!

00:12:40.210 --> 00:12:41.500
Yeah!

00:12:43.210 --> 00:12:45.920
Sorry, but we're closed for the day...

00:12:46.960 --> 00:12:48.580
Wait, Ms. Elyn?

00:12:49.210 --> 00:12:50.500
Good evening.

00:12:50.500 --> 00:12:52.500
What brings you here
at this time of night?

00:12:52.500 --> 00:12:56.000
Well, there was a bit of something
I wanted to discuss with you...

00:12:57.460 --> 00:12:58.580
To discuss...?

00:13:16.710 --> 00:13:18.210
This is narsnacchi!

00:13:18.210 --> 00:13:20.170
You rarely ever see it!

00:13:20.170 --> 00:13:21.290
How lucky!

00:13:22.920 --> 00:13:26.380
Ooh, to think I'd find tyneltac
in a place like this!

00:13:26.380 --> 00:13:28.420
I almost overlooked it!

00:13:29.460 --> 00:13:32.960
Wow, this moss is blue powder!

00:13:32.960 --> 00:13:35.420
Normally it's green, but this is blue!

00:13:35.420 --> 00:13:37.540
It'll definitely be worth something!

00:13:37.960 --> 00:13:40.250
That's the forest for you!

00:13:40.250 --> 00:13:42.080
It's a treasure trove of ingredients!

00:13:42.080 --> 00:13:43.040
That's amazing...

00:13:43.040 --> 00:13:44.830
To think you can find this many
valuable ingredients

00:13:44.830 --> 00:13:47.080
when you have the necessary knowledge...

00:13:47.080 --> 00:13:49.580
At this rate, we could end up with
a haul worth multiple times

00:13:49.580 --> 00:13:51.000
what we normally get.

00:13:51.000 --> 00:13:53.080
That's good to hear, but still...

00:13:54.580 --> 00:13:56.250
What about the investigation?

00:13:56.250 --> 00:13:57.790
Whoops, that's right.

00:13:58.000 --> 00:14:00.250
That was the main job here.

00:14:01.420 --> 00:14:03.710
An investigation into
the hellflame grizzlies?

00:14:03.710 --> 00:14:04.790
Yes...

00:14:04.790 --> 00:14:09.000
We still don't know the cause behind
their frenzy from before, right?

00:14:09.000 --> 00:14:11.460
There's no guarantee that the
same thing won't happen again.

00:14:11.460 --> 00:14:17.080
We asked the local lord to have
an investigation done. However...

00:14:17.080 --> 00:14:18.290
The local lord...

00:14:18.290 --> 00:14:20.210
Yokuo Kirk, huh?

00:14:20.420 --> 00:14:24.210
But we received a response today
that there was no need for one,

00:14:24.210 --> 00:14:26.540
as the damages weren't severe.

00:14:26.540 --> 00:14:27.540
That's awful!

00:14:27.880 --> 00:14:29.710
We only avoided a huge incident

00:14:29.710 --> 00:14:32.580
because Ms. Sarasa and everyone
worked so hard!

00:14:32.580 --> 00:14:34.830
So that's why you're coming to us?

00:14:34.830 --> 00:14:36.290
I'm sorry.

00:14:36.290 --> 00:14:39.250
There wasn't anyone else
I could consult with about it...

00:14:39.250 --> 00:14:40.290
Alright.

00:14:40.290 --> 00:14:41.080
Huh?

00:14:41.080 --> 00:14:45.080
I have an idea as to what
may have caused the frenzy.

00:14:45.080 --> 00:14:49.630
And since it will probably require
going past the depths of the forest,

00:14:49.630 --> 00:14:53.040
we'll also be able to get ahold of
plenty of rare ingredients.

00:14:55.210 --> 00:14:57.670
Just leave the investigation to us.

00:14:57.670 --> 00:14:59.790
We'll absolutely figure out the cause,

00:14:59.790 --> 00:15:02.420
and earn plenty of money
while we're at it!

00:15:02.630 --> 00:15:03.750
Ms. Owner...!

00:15:03.750 --> 00:15:05.170
Thank you!

00:15:15.750 --> 00:15:19.500
I truly am sorry for all of this, Ms. Owner.

00:15:19.500 --> 00:15:22.710
Come on, I already told you
not to worry about it, didn't I?

00:15:22.710 --> 00:15:27.630
And I am also terribly grateful
for how considerate you've been,

00:15:27.630 --> 00:15:30.420
not telling Andre's group
about the debt.

00:15:32.040 --> 00:15:34.420
It's not the sort of thing to go
spreading around.

00:15:34.420 --> 00:15:38.790
But I get the feeling that Andre's group
has more or less picked up on things.

00:15:39.630 --> 00:15:43.880
They may know, but be helping out
without saying anything.

00:15:45.710 --> 00:15:46.920
I...

00:15:51.170 --> 00:15:52.330
I...

00:15:58.920 --> 00:16:00.250
Let's give our all!

00:16:00.250 --> 00:16:03.250
We'll finally reach the mountain tomorrow!

00:16:10.830 --> 00:16:12.710
We finally made it.

00:16:13.170 --> 00:16:16.170
So there are hellflame grizzlies
on this mountain?

00:16:16.170 --> 00:16:18.790
To be more precise, there were.

00:16:18.790 --> 00:16:21.080
At least as long as that pack
which attacked us

00:16:21.080 --> 00:16:23.750
didn't come from somewhere far away.

00:16:23.920 --> 00:16:27.330
In other words, the question of
why they left this place

00:16:27.330 --> 00:16:30.960
is tied to our investigation
into their frenzy?

00:16:30.960 --> 00:16:35.580
There aren't really any signs of
the mountain collapsing... I think.

00:16:35.580 --> 00:16:38.330
We don't know what it
looked like originally, after all.

00:16:38.330 --> 00:16:40.000
And there isn't any smoke
coming from it,

00:16:40.000 --> 00:16:42.330
so it doesn't seem to have
become unusually active.

00:16:42.540 --> 00:16:47.080
Then is the cause the flame stones
they eat running out after all...?

00:16:47.080 --> 00:16:49.420
Still, why did that happen?

00:16:49.420 --> 00:16:53.460
Hey Sarasa, it's not going to
suddenly blow or anything, is it?

00:16:53.460 --> 00:16:57.630
I can't say with absolute certainty,
but I believe we should be fine.

00:16:57.630 --> 00:16:59.920
Unless we're incredibly unlucky, that is.

00:16:59.920 --> 00:17:03.130
Luck, is it? I can't say
I'm feeling all that confident.

00:17:03.130 --> 00:17:05.130
Because you almost died once, right?

00:17:05.130 --> 00:17:07.290
But you were saved in the end,

00:17:07.290 --> 00:17:09.330
so I don't think you
need to be that worried.

00:17:09.330 --> 00:17:10.420
Besides...!

00:17:11.460 --> 00:17:14.130
We've got Sarasa here with us now!

00:17:14.130 --> 00:17:15.210
We'll be fine!

00:17:15.210 --> 00:17:16.580
Who, me?

00:17:16.580 --> 00:17:18.580
Are you saying I'm lucky?

00:17:18.580 --> 00:17:20.880
No, we are!

00:17:20.880 --> 00:17:23.540
We're real lucky to have met you!

00:17:23.540 --> 00:17:24.540
Huh?

00:17:24.880 --> 00:17:27.540
Even when we were attacked by
raging hellflame grizzlies...

00:17:27.540 --> 00:17:30.500
And when we suffered terribly from
honey we didn't really understand...

00:17:30.500 --> 00:17:34.460
Yes! It all worked out because
you were there, Ms. Owner!

00:17:34.460 --> 00:17:35.580
That's right.

00:17:35.580 --> 00:17:37.790
We're crazy lucky!

00:17:38.000 --> 00:17:42.250
It makes me a bit happy,
hearing you say all that...

00:17:51.580 --> 00:17:54.790
It feels like we've climbed quite a bit,

00:17:54.790 --> 00:17:58.630
but there don't seem to be many
flame stones about even here.

00:17:58.920 --> 00:18:02.580
I guess we'll just have to gather
what we can and head on back.

00:18:02.580 --> 00:18:07.080
Hey Sarasa, shouldn't we look for
somewhere we can gather more?

00:18:07.080 --> 00:18:11.040
You normally tend to find lots of them
laying around where the ground is hot.

00:18:11.040 --> 00:18:12.750
Ooh, then what about that spot
where it's steaming?

00:18:12.750 --> 00:18:13.580
Stop!
Ooh, then what about that spot<b>
</b>where it's steaming?<b></b>

00:18:13.580 --> 00:18:14.250
Huh?

00:18:14.250 --> 00:18:16.750
It's true that the temperature
would be high there,

00:18:16.750 --> 00:18:18.380
but there's poisonous gas in the air

00:18:18.380 --> 00:18:20.210
that would knock you out
in a single breath,

00:18:20.210 --> 00:18:22.290
and there's a danger
of extremely heated vapor

00:18:22.290 --> 00:18:24.710
and boiling water
suddenly spurting out.

00:18:26.630 --> 00:18:30.290
Let's just gather from where
it's safe for now.

00:18:30.750 --> 00:18:32.290
If we absolutely need more,

00:18:32.290 --> 00:18:34.670
we'll come back when we're
better prepared.

00:18:35.670 --> 00:18:37.290
What is it, Sarasa?

00:18:37.290 --> 00:18:38.710
Over near the steam...

00:18:39.500 --> 00:18:40.880
Something's there.

00:18:47.420 --> 00:18:50.420
That's one big lizard. What is it?

00:18:50.420 --> 00:18:52.420
A lava lizard.

00:18:52.420 --> 00:18:54.920
Also known as a pseudo-salamander.

00:18:54.920 --> 00:18:57.830
That's a pretty strong sounding name!

00:18:58.040 --> 00:19:02.000
Well, they're not as strong as
the name implies, but they're tough.

00:19:02.460 --> 00:19:07.290
The skin on their backs is sturdy enough
to deflect hellflame grizzly claws.

00:19:07.540 --> 00:19:09.830
On top of that they can breath fire,

00:19:09.830 --> 00:19:12.830
and they can launch incredibly
powerful attacks with their tails.

00:19:13.080 --> 00:19:14.920
Sounds troublesome...

00:19:14.920 --> 00:19:19.080
So did those lizards drive
the hellflame grizzlies away?

00:19:19.080 --> 00:19:20.420
In all likelihood...

00:19:20.710 --> 00:19:24.420
Lava lizards actually primarily eat
flame stones as well.

00:19:24.420 --> 00:19:28.750
However, they have a greater resistance
to heat than hellflame grizzlies.

00:19:28.750 --> 00:19:30.000
I see.

00:19:30.000 --> 00:19:35.460
So the lava lizards can eat flame stones
where the hellflame grizzlies can too,

00:19:35.460 --> 00:19:37.500
but the reverse isn't true.

00:19:37.500 --> 00:19:39.460
After losing the struggle for survival

00:19:39.460 --> 00:19:42.130
the hellflame grizzlies were
driven from their home,

00:19:42.130 --> 00:19:44.330
and as a result,
they went into a frenzy...

00:19:44.330 --> 00:19:46.830
Yes, that's likely the case.

00:19:47.580 --> 00:19:52.710
So that technically means the investigation
Elyn ordered is finished, right?

00:19:52.710 --> 00:19:56.170
Yes. There aren't any actual
hellflame grizzlies around,

00:19:56.170 --> 00:20:00.380
so we now know another frenzy
would be highly unlikely.

00:20:00.380 --> 00:20:01.420
But...!

00:20:01.580 --> 00:20:03.130
Since we came all this way,

00:20:03.130 --> 00:20:05.420
you want to earn a little more
before heading back, right?

00:20:07.420 --> 00:20:11.500
It's true that ingredients from
lava lizards do demand quite a price.

00:20:11.750 --> 00:20:14.710
But you haven't ever
hunted them before, have you?

00:20:14.710 --> 00:20:16.920
Right! It's my first time even seeing one!

00:20:18.420 --> 00:20:20.500
They generally move at a relaxed pace,

00:20:20.500 --> 00:20:22.830
so as long as you don't
encounter too many at once,

00:20:22.830 --> 00:20:24.460
it shouldn't be all that dangerous.

00:20:24.460 --> 00:20:27.540
Still, watch out for their breath and tails.

00:20:27.750 --> 00:20:32.460
Their tails possess enough strength
to break an adult leg,

00:20:32.460 --> 00:20:36.830
so don't go thinking you should
approach them from behind and attack.

00:20:36.830 --> 00:20:39.000
And it's said that when they're
feeling endangered

00:20:39.000 --> 00:20:40.750
they'll try to lure their enemies
into boiling lakes,

00:20:40.750 --> 00:20:42.460
so be careful not to follow them too far.

00:20:42.460 --> 00:20:44.830
Th-that sounds rather tough.

00:20:44.830 --> 00:20:45.830
Yeah...

00:20:45.830 --> 00:20:48.170
So how should we actually
take them down?

00:20:48.170 --> 00:20:50.460
Well then, why don't I show you?

00:20:51.040 --> 00:20:54.670
You should aim for the spot on
their stomach where it's a bit softer.

00:20:54.670 --> 00:20:57.790
The top of their body is so sturdy
that swords won't pierce through.

00:20:58.250 --> 00:21:02.170
So, even if you attack
from above like so...!

00:21:04.080 --> 00:21:06.290
Well, that's how it turns out.

00:21:06.290 --> 00:21:10.080
So you have to attack from the side
or flip them over to cut them.

00:21:10.080 --> 00:21:13.460
No way, you totally cut it!
Its head even fell off!

00:21:13.580 --> 00:21:15.880
Huh? How strange.

00:21:15.880 --> 00:21:20.130
I figured I would show you how you'll be
repelled if you try to do it like that.

00:21:21.710 --> 00:21:25.080
She really is on a whole other level...

00:21:25.080 --> 00:21:27.960
She's way stronger than we are...

00:21:27.960 --> 00:21:31.040
N-no, it's just that
this sword is so sturdy.

00:21:31.040 --> 00:21:33.210
That would normally never work.

00:21:34.380 --> 00:21:36.290
I already knew it,

00:21:36.290 --> 00:21:39.290
but I'm terribly ashamed by
my own lack of training...

00:21:42.580 --> 00:21:43.960
Lava lizards?!

00:21:44.790 --> 00:21:46.630
A whole swarm!

00:21:46.750 --> 00:21:48.540
M-Ms. Owner!

00:21:56.960 --> 00:21:58.540
M-Ms. Owner!

00:22:03.170 --> 00:22:04.710
A-amazing...!

00:22:10.630 --> 00:22:11.790
Sorry about that.

00:22:11.790 --> 00:22:14.670
I never expected there to be more
hiding around like that...

00:22:14.670 --> 00:22:17.330
I should have been more cautious
in regards to my surroundings.

00:22:17.330 --> 00:22:19.670
There's no beating you, Ms. Owner.

00:22:19.880 --> 00:22:23.040
Ms. Owner, I'm the one
who should be apologizing!

00:22:23.040 --> 00:22:27.130
This happened because I carelessly placed
my hand where I shouldn't have...!

00:22:27.130 --> 00:22:28.830
What are you saying?

00:22:28.830 --> 00:22:30.130
You should be happy!

00:22:30.130 --> 00:22:32.420
Look how many we took down!

00:22:34.170 --> 00:22:36.670
Still, something's strange here...

00:22:37.000 --> 00:22:41.330
That many lava lizards being about
is incredibly abnormal.

00:22:42.710 --> 00:22:46.080
Hopefully this isn't an omen
of something bad to come...

00:22:48.790 --> 00:22:50.130
A-an earthquake?!

00:22:52.920 --> 00:22:55.750
Hey, this is no joke!

00:22:55.750 --> 00:22:57.920
Hide by those rocks! Hurry!

00:23:10.880 --> 00:23:12.040
Ms. Owner...?

00:23:23.080 --> 00:23:25.040
What a massive hole.

00:23:25.040 --> 00:23:27.420
It must have opened with that eruption.

00:23:27.580 --> 00:23:29.420
Watch out, everyone.

00:23:31.670 --> 00:23:34.750
There's a salamander down there!

